# Runtime dependencies. Exact pins live in base.txt, dev.txt, prod.txt.
# Lock for Linux / Python 3.12 (the image) from any machine, with uv:
#
#   bash scripts/lock.sh            # keeps current pins, adds what is new
#   bash scripts/lock.sh --upgrade  # newest versions inside the ranges
#
# Same options as the Zeneonix site (--allow-unsafe --no-emit-index-url --strip-extras).
# The script resolves the private core from its local clone at the pinned SHA
# (../zeneon-cms), then writes the ssh URL below back into the locks.

# The CMS core, pinned by commit SHA (D2): the tip of main on 2026-11-10. Core work for
# TIC (#14 hCaptcha, #15 routing, #16 review-by) lands on a branch and moves this pin.
# No "mcp" extra: TIC runs no MCP container in V1 (master plan 16).
zeneon-cms @ git+ssh://git@github.com/daryabsb/zeneon-cms.git@ae597a1b2a3b4237ce2ed788100da5b602ca87d8

# Series pins. The core declares compatible ranges; these keep the site on the LTS
# series it was tested with (same as the Zeneonix site).
